# Glint-Web Rules

Use this editor to turn real screenshots into polished store frames.

## Must keep

1. Left sidebar: Templates · Assets · Frames · Export (workflow)
2. Right sidebar Design: device frame dropdown, graphic preview tiles, font dropdown, canvas
3. Center: frames board (1-10 store-size artboards), not an infinite canvas
4. Device frames must fill screenshot insets without gaps
5. Export sizes stay store-correct (Play / iOS / iPad presets)
6. ZIP naming: `{appName}.zip` when app name exists, else `glint.zip`
7. View handoff: after Preview/Export, Copy for Glint View embeds `data:` screens

## Assets behavior

- Session import reads `session.json` and maps ordered `screens` to PNG files
- Prefer one device in Capture for Web frames (primary device in session.json)
- Frames panel: reorder layers; device right-click to import/clear screenshot

## Guardrails

- Real UI only - never invent product screens
- Soft-launch path: Capture/Bridge → Web → View (preview only)
